==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Brainwashed Sexy Legs Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Brainwashed Macho Legs Cat''' when obtained from [[Devilish Strides (Merciless)]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Brainwashed Gross Cat is similar to [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] as both cats have the same role: sniping backliner enemies with a powerful pseudo-area attack. Better yet, they have nearly identical stats when hypermaxed, meaning Brainwashed Gross will not lose relevance in the late game.

Brainwashed Gross spawns a surge that hits enemies up to 3 times rather than once. This means that his surge can have up to thrice the strength of Manic Macho Legs' waves, doing great damage to bosses and peons that are unfortunate enough to cross its path. This high backline DPS comes at the cost of the surges' RNG-fueled spawn location. Stacking can somewhat solve this issue, though, like with Manic Macho Legs, this is a long process, and even the surge may not spawn at a desired location, making Manic Macho Legs a somewhat better alternative for reliability. Using them together remains a valid option, however.

Brainwashed Gross's Evolved form attacks slightly faster than the Normal form. Always use the Evolved form until you receive its True Form.

=== '''True Form''' ===
All Brainwashed Gross gains from true form is an increased surge level. This actually increases its potential DPS by quite a lot, as their surge can now have quadruple the strength of Manic Macho Legs' waves. While this isn't the flashiest or most exciting true form upgrade, it's still satisfactory and improves upon a cat that was already quite good and viable in many scenarios.

{{Job|Classification = Sniper & Midranger}}

